<title>CYPRUS: More Western, Asian oil cos interested in Iraq - MEES.</title>
<headline>More Western, Asian oil cos interested in Iraq - MEES.</headline>
<dateline>NICOSIA 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Several more Western and Asian oil firms have expressed interest to the Iraqi oil authorities in upstream involvement &quot;as and when circumstances become appropriate,&quot; the Middle East Economic Survey (MEES) said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;It is understood that in addition to the over 40 firms reported earlier as having held talks with Iraq's Ministry of Oil, some 17 new companies have made contacts with Baghdad recently,&quot; MEES said.</p>
<p>These included Mobil, Conoco, Chevron, Occidental, Arco, Exxon, Texaco and Coastal of the United States.</p>
<p>They also included British Petroleum and BG British Gas, Japan's Inpex, Idemitsu and Sumitomo, Vietnam Oil and Gas Co, India's Reliance Industries, Hungary's Hanpetro and the Tunisian firm Setcar, the newsletter said.</p>
</text>
